ion."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.9x net debt to EBITDA ($1.0B of cash against $46.5B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 5.4x.","The current ratio of 0.97 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 7.9% over 3 years, 8.0% over 5 years and 6.7% over 10 years.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.4x, 6.5% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 18, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 4.4% on average."],"own":["Insiders own 17.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 82%.","It returns 10.4% a year to shareholders (9.7% in buybacks and 0.6% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 7.1% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 230,000 employees, each generates about $329K of revenue, in line with the Healthcare median, and productivity has risen 6.9% a year.","That works out to $33K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $7.5M (23x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":89,"head":"Invest: trades 33% below fair value of $737; ROIC 24.5% vs WACC 8.0%.","pros":["Model rating BUY (composite 60, gates 17/24)","Trades 33% below fair value of $737","ROIC 24.5% vs WACC 8.0%","FCF margin 10.2%","Revenue grew 8.0%/yr over 5y"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":626.16,"vc":{"base":736.66,"base_src":"dcf","bear":528.57,"bull":1048.44,"alt_median":365.0,"n_alt":2,"gap":1.0182,"dispersion":0.0994,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 102% above the other models' median ($365)"]},"med":{"pe":25.5,"ev_ebitda":15.7195,"pfcf":23.7283,"pb":3.5607,"roic":-0.1181,"gross_margin":0.5566,"fcf_margin":0.0285